{"title":"Career Roadmap · AYUSH Medical Officer","role":"AYUSH Medical Officer","summary":"An AYUSH Medical Officer is a qualified healthcare professional who provides services within the AYUSH healthcare system, with responsibilities depending on the employing organization, applicable regulations, and the specific post.","facts":{"Current degree":"BAMS (Ayurveda)","Course":"Ayurvedic Medicine & Surgery"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An AYUSH Medical Officer is a qualified healthcare professional who provides services within the AYUSH healthcare system, with responsibilities depending on the employing organization, applicable regulations, and the specific post."},{"type":"p","text":"For a BAMS graduate, the role can involve:"},{"type":"h","text":"Ayurvedic patient consultation"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical assessment within the permitted scope of practice"},{"type":"h","text":"Ayurvedic diagnosis and treatment planning"},{"type":"h","text":"Prescription of appropriate Ayurvedic medicines"},{"type":"h","text":"Preventive and promotive healthcare"},{"type":"h","text":"Public-health activities"},{"type":"h","text":"Health camps"},{"type":"h","text":"Community healthcare"},{"type":"h","text":"Documentation and reporting"},{"type":"h","text":"Health education"},{"type":"h","text":"Referral of cases requiring other medical expertise"},{"type":"h","text":"Participation in government AYUSH programs"},{"type":"h","text":"Potential employers include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Government AYUSH hospitals"},{"type":"h","text":"Government dispensaries"},{"type":"h","text":"Primary/community healthcare programs"},{"type":"h","text":"AYUSH departments"},{"type":"h","text":"Ayurvedic hospitals"},{"type":"h","text":"Wellness centres"},{"type":"h","text":"Research institutions"},{"type":"h","text":"Public-health programs"},{"type":"h","text":"Private healthcare organizations"},{"type":"h","text":"Integrative healthcare facilities"},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Eligibility for an AYUSH Medical Officer post depends on the recruitment notification, recognized qualification, registration requirements, applicable state/national rules, and the nature of the position. Students should verify the current eligibility criteria for the specific post."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"BAMS"},{"type":"h","text":"Compulsory Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Professional Registration"},{"type":"h","text":"AYUSH / Government Healthcare Internship & Exam Preparation"},{"type":"h","text":"AYUSH Medical Officer"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Medical Officer / Clinical Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Administrative / Program Responsibilities"},{"type":"h","text":"District / State-Level AYUSH Roles"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Administration / Program Leadership"},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative pathway:"},{"type":"h","text":"BAMS"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Experience"},{"type":"h","text":"AYUSH Hospital / Private Practice"},{"type":"h","text":"Government AYUSH Medical Officer"},{"type":"h","text":"PG Specialization / Public Health"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Clinical / Administrative Role"}]},{"heading":"BAMS Academic Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Early Years — Ayurvedic & Biomedical Sciences"},{"type":"h","text":"Build a strong foundation in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Ayurveda fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"Sanskrit terminology relevant to Ayurveda"},{"type":"h","text":"Anatomy"},{"type":"h","text":"Physiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Ayurvedic physiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Ayurvedic pharmacology"},{"type":"h","text":"Dravyaguna"},{"type":"h","text":"Pathology"},{"type":"h","text":"Pharmacology"},{"type":"h","text":"Biochemistry"},{"type":"h","text":"Microbiology"},{"type":"h","text":"The goal is to understand both:"},{"type":"h","text":"Traditional Ayurvedic concepts + Modern biomedical f